FEATURES             Location/Qualifiers
     promoter        1..56
                     /label="tetR/tetA promoters"
                     /synonym="tetR/tetA promoters"
                     /synonym="Tn10 tetA promoter"
                     /synonym="tetA/tetR control region"
                     /note="The Tn10 divergent tetA/tetR control region: 56 bp
                     carrying the PtetA promoter, the overlapping PtetR
                     promoter, and the two TetR operators tetO1 and tetO2. The
                     tetR promoters are not declared as sub-features. Daniels &
                     Bertrand 1985 describe two, tetPR1 and tetPR2; Gulland &
                     Hillen 1992 find that more than 95% of tetR mRNA in vivo
                     starts at PR2, at a run of five A's, and the J01830 record
                     places the tetR mRNA 5' end at 1544 -- that run (J01830
                     1540-1544 on the tetR strand), one base outside this 56 bp
                     window. No accessible source gives the -35/-10 positions of
                     either promoter. The reading consistent with the PR2 start
                     (-35 TGGTAA at J01830 1574-1579, -10 TAGAGT at 1551-1556 on
                     the tetR strand, 17 bp spacer, +1 7 bases on) has 7 of 12
                     consensus bases, too few to predict. Sub-features this part
                     carried before put the tetR +1 at J01830 1564, inside
                     tetO1, which the record and the five-A start contradict for
                     PR2; whether they described PR1 is not established. The
                     pRAB vectors' tetR promoter, a modified form of this
                     region, is the catalog part PtetR* (pRAB)."
                     /db_xref="SO:0000167"
                     /db_xref="GenBank:J01830"
